  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Protection, Living Conditions, and Reducing the Vulnerabilities of IDPs and Host Communities among the Flood-Affected Populations in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heavy rainfalls, accompanied by strong winds alongside overflooding of rivers and the opening of the dam gates in Cameroon, led to the flooding of communities in Nigeria, causing serious damage to shelter and infrastructures within the internally displaced persons camps and host communities. The floods destroyed farmlands, shelters, water, sanitation and hygiene infrastructures, and sources of livelihood and caused the further displacement of populations. The project aims to contribute towards reducing vulnerabilities and improve the living conditions of flood-affected population in Nigeria. This is achieved by employing a multisectoral and multilevel approach to ensure assistance is provided to flood-affected populations, including displaced populations, returnees, and host communities. Activities providing direct assistance to beneficiaries are being implemented in displacement sites as well as host communities, from the following sectors of assistance: Camp Coordination and Camp Management, Shelter/Non-food Items, WASH, Early Recovery and Livelihoods, Health, and Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS).</narrative>
  </description>
